             excitement like dogs, but many cats clearly distinguish their favorite people from strangers.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">
           <span>Why do cats knead with their paws?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-4" hidden>
           <p>
             Kneading begins in kittenhood to stimulate milk flow and often carries into adulthood as a comfort
             behavior. Many cats knead when they feel safe, cozy, and content.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-5">
           <span>How can you tell if a cat is stressed?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="faq-5" hidden>
           <p>
             Signs of stress can include hiding, flattened ears, tail flicking, unusual vocalizing, changes in
             appetite, or avoiding the litter box. Sudden behavior changes are worth watching closely.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>
     </section>
